  "note": "The source of the connection between cooking and presumption is uncertain. Psalm 19 uses a masculine plural which can refer to insolent people or, in context, presumptuous acts.\n\nThe corpus has no accepted זיף root key, so this separate homograph entry retains the BDB bridge root זיד while its sense is the Ziph place-name and must not be read as the presumptuousness root.\n\nMerged from `zid`, `zif` on 2026-11-20: one root, one entry."
